              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">6b9507eb-1298-489e-98e0-7f2f82818193</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10"></item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">ROOF RIB / 2D TEACHING CASE / TopOptLab 0.4
Start: read LEGGIMI.md and the slides. Units: mm, N, MPa. World XY: Y is UP.
1 BASELINE FEM &gt; 2 OPTIMIZATION &gt; 3 FINAL VERIFICATION. Press one RUN at a time.
Five independent load cases; each contains six point resultants plus self-weight.
Geometry is internalized: the file works without selecting Rhino objects.
Keep the reference h=100 mm for the first run. If h changes, set Radius=180/h cells and rerun all stages.
This is an elastic planar plate concept; it does not check buckling, anchorage or building-code compliance.</item>
                  </items>
